```

Final focused result: **16 passed, 0 failed, 9 ignored, 0 measured**. The
passing count excludes ignored child fixtures. The parent first checked
each valid prefix and the exact checker rejection for its defective next
transition, then launched each deliberately defective child. All nine child
processes exited with status 101 and the intended diagnostic:

  dropped lease reopens participation:
    no modeled transition may reopen participation
  handoff before receiver acceptance:
    supervisor ownership transferred before acceptance
  ABA tuple equality after lease loss:
    tuple equality cannot restore a lost or invalidated lease
  late completion clears Unknown:
    completion cleared unresolved or conflicting obligation
  duplicate completion clears conflict:
    completion cleared unresolved or conflicting obligation
  mutation without post-ack revalidation:
    protected mutation requires post-ack tuple revalidation
  operation cancellation after accepted handoff:
    operation cancellation forbids protected mutation
  pre-existing pending work omitted:
    protected mutation lacks live owner lease or resolved obligations
  late visible publication after cancellation:
    operation cancellation forbids protected mutation

Positive traces include valid revalidation immediately before mutation,
accepted supervisor ownership after initiator task end, pre-existing work
resolved before mutation, publication visibility observed after cancellation
without gaining authority, uncertain publication after owner loss, and
pending/known outcomes retained through modeled restart. These are
deterministic test-model traces only, not process or deployment evidence.

